{"id":"chatcmpl-fab5029f-5286-4177-8b98-b23d9cfb49f1","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246721,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first approach for medical image interpretation where the imaging view (lateral) complicates side assignment. The key insight is recognizing that lateral views require explicit anatomical landmark reasoning to distinguish left vs. right, and that expert claims should be validated against those landmarks before finalizing. The pattern generalizes to any task where image orientation or labeling creates ambiguity in spatial reasoning.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When image metadata (e.g., view label) indicates a non-standard projection, explicitly request reasoning about how anatomical landmarks disambiguate spatial claims rather than accepting side assignments at face value.\",\n    \"Use a domain expert tool for initial interpretation, then route the proposed answer through a verification step that checks whether the reasoning is grounded in valid view-specific landmarks.\",\n    \"Flag high-risk claims where the answer depends on distinguishing left/right or other spatial attributes that are ambiguous in the given view, and require confirmation before finalizing.\",\n    \"Separate the interpretation step (what finding is present) from the validation step (is the side/orientation assignment justified), even when both concern the same image.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Identify the projection/view first; for lateral or oblique views, require explicit landmark-based reasoning (e.g., gastric bubble, posterior costophrenic angle) before accepting left/right assignments.\",\n    \"Ambiguous spatial reasoning tasks\": \"When orientation is non-obvious, ask the expert to state which cues distinguish the options, then verify those cues are valid for the given view.\",\n    \"Expert-tool orchestration\": \"Pair an interpretation tool with a verification tool that audits the reasoning chain, especially when the answer hinges on a single ambiguous attribute.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the imaging view/projection and whether left/right can be reliably distinguished from it.\",\n    \"Verify that the proposed side assignment cites valid view-specific anatomical landmarks rather than assumption.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":545,"total_tokens":953,"completion_tokens":408,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":545},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":408}}}